      "kind": "numeric",
      "scenario": "Work out, as a decimal:\n\n$$\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{4}$$",
      "answer": 0.75,
      "unit": "",
      "tolerance": 0.001,
      "hints": ["Rewrite $\\tfrac12$ as $\\tfrac24$ so both have denominator 4.", "Add the numerators: $\\tfrac24 + \\tfrac14 = \\tfrac34$."],
      "solution": "Use a common denominator of 4:\n\n$$\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{2}{4} + \\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{3}{4} = 0.75$$",
      "equationsUsed": ["\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{3}{4}"],
