      "tags": ["fractions", "multiply"],
      "kind": "numeric",
      "scenario": "Work out, as a decimal:\n\n$$\\frac{2}{3} \\times \\frac{3}{4}$$",
      "answer": 0.5,
      "unit": "",
      "tolerance": 0.001,
      "hints": ["Multiply straight across: tops × tops, bottoms × bottoms.", "$\\tfrac{6}{12}$ simplifies to $\\tfrac12$."],
      "solution": "Multiply across and simplify:\n\n$$\\frac{2}{3}\\times\\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{6}{12} = \\frac{1}{2} = 0.5$$\n\n(You could cancel the 3's first to get $\\tfrac12$ directly.)",
      "equationsUsed": ["\\frac{2}{3}\\times\\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{1}{2}"],
      "conceptLink": "al02"
