      "title": "Divide fractions",
      "tags": ["fractions", "divide"],
      "kind": "numeric",
      "scenario": "Work out, as a decimal:\n\n$$\\frac{3}{4} \\div \\frac{1}{2}$$",
      "answer": 1.5,
      "unit": "",
      "tolerance": 0.001,
      "hints": ["Keep, change, flip: $\\tfrac34 \\times \\tfrac21$.", "$\\tfrac{6}{4} = \\tfrac32$."],
      "solution": "Flip the divisor and multiply:\n\n$$\\frac{3}{4}\\div\\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{3}{4}\\times\\frac{2}{1} = \\frac{6}{4} = \\frac{3}{2} = 1.5$$\n\nDividing by a number below 1 makes the result bigger.",
      "equationsUsed": ["\\frac{3}{4}\\div\\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{3}{2}"],
      "conceptLink": "al02"
