      "kind": "open",
      "scenario": "Simplify\n\n$$\\frac{\\;2/3\\;}{\\;4/9\\;}$$\n\nGive a single simplified fraction.",
      "hints": ["A fraction over a fraction is a division: $\\tfrac23 \\div \\tfrac49$.", "Keep, change, flip, then cancel."],
      "solution": "Rewrite as a division and flip:\n\n$$\\frac{2/3}{4/9} = \\frac{2}{3}\\div\\frac{4}{9} = \\frac{2}{3}\\times\\frac{9}{4} = \\frac{18}{12} = \\frac{3}{2}$$",
      "equationsUsed": ["\\frac{2}{3}\\times\\frac{9}{4} = \\frac{3}{2}"],
      "conceptLink": "al02"
