      "tolerance": 0.001,
      "hints": ["Do the bracket first: $\\tfrac12 + \\tfrac13 = \\tfrac56$.", "Then $\\tfrac56 \\div \\tfrac56 = 1$."],
      "solution": "Bracket first (common denominator 6), then divide:\n\n$$\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{3}{6} + \\frac{2}{6} = \\frac{5}{6}$$\n$$\\frac{5}{6} \\div \\frac{5}{6} = \\frac{5}{6}\\times\\frac{6}{5} = 1$$",
      "equationsUsed": ["\\frac{5}{6}\\div\\frac{5}{6} = 1"],
      "conceptLink": "al02"
